WEBVTT

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.141
AI can give students the answer.

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:06.434
But can they teach it?

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:11.617
Selecting the right answer is not the same as understanding it.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:18.012
chalkcast turns any assignment into a recorded demonstration of understanding.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.793
Students draw, label, diagram, and solve on a digital whiteboard, while they explain their work out loud.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.629
You see their face. You hear their explanation. You watch their model take shape.

00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:41.310
They explain why it is correct, how it works, and how the concepts connect, by designing the connections and the underlying model themselves.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.069
Keep your existing assignments. You set the problem, add your rubric, and choose a time limit.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:53.158
Students just click a link. No accounts, and nothing to install.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:01:00.427
When they finish, the recording and a whiteboard PDF come back through your learning management system.

00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:08.802
Short on time? Choose a ready-made question from the built-in bank. Each one comes with a starter rubric you can edit.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:19.488
Want to follow up on work a student turned in? Send a defense question. It stays hidden until they press begin, and recording starts at the same moment.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.708
It works across disciplines. Anatomy, chemistry, nursing, math, and more.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:35.648
Student privacy comes first. No student accounts. Nothing stored. Every video stays on the student's own device until they upload it.

00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:43.070
You don't need to eliminate AI from education. You need assessments that ask students to do the thinking.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.532
Don't just assess the answer. Assess the understanding.

00:01:48.633 --> 00:01:57.296
